# What the build context is allowed to contain.
#
# The Dockerfile only ever COPYs three things — requirements.txt, src/ and ui/.
# Everything listed here is either secret (.env), enormous (downloaded videos,
# model weights), or noise the build daemon has no reason to see. Keeping the
# context small also keeps `fly deploy --remote-only` fast, since the whole
# context is uploaded to the remote builder on every deploy.
#
# PATTERN SEMANTICS — the thing that makes these files silently useless:
# patterns are matched against each file's path RELATIVE TO THE CONTEXT ROOT,
# and a lone `*` never crosses a `/`. So `__pycache__/` matches ONLY a
# root-level __pycache__ — not src/__pycache__, not src/api/__pycache__. Any
# pattern meant to apply at any depth needs the `**/` prefix. Patterns without
# it below are deliberately root-anchored (data/, .git/, fly.toml, ...).
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: requirements.txt, requirements-clip.txt (the torch
# stack the fat app image and Dockerfile.clip install), src/, ui/.

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never in a build context. Runtime config arrives as env vars / Fly secrets;
# compose mounts .env at run time (see config.py's load_dotenv note), which is
# a volume mount, not a copy — so excluding it here changes nothing at runtime.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/cookies.txt
# The whole secrets/ tree, not just cookies.txt: it's mounted at run time
# (docker-compose mounts ./secrets read-only into worker + seed) and anything
# else parked there — a service-account JSON, a proxy list — has no business
# being uploaded to a remote builder either.
secrets/

# ── Runtime data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Raw uploads, extracted frames, local-provider storage, local Qdrant. This is
# the directory that makes an un-ignored context gigabytes wide.
data/
qdrant_storage/

# ── Model caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The image downloads its own weights at runtime into /root/.cache (the
# hf_cache volume in compose). A host-side cache must never be baked in.
**/.cache/
**/*.pt
**/*.onnx
**/*.safetensors

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bytecode is the one that actually bloats the shipped layers: src/ is ~1.3 MB
# on disk but only ~350 KB of .py, and the rest is stale .pyc — including
# cpython-314 artifacts that a python:3.11 image can't even load. Excluding it
# also stops a local test run from invalidating the COPY cache layer.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# ── VCS and CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# ── Docs and non-shipping code ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing in the image reads markdown. examples/ and benchmark/ are run from a
# clone, not from the container.
**/*.md
LICENSE
NOTICE
examples/
benchmark/

# ── Host-side deploy configs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by flyctl / docker compose on the HOST; the container never sees them.
# (Dockerfile, Dockerfile.clip and .dockerignore are intentionally NOT listed —
# the builder needs them, and excluding them buys nothing.)
fly*.toml
docker-compose*.yml

# ── Editor and OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
